<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">

    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Subtitle">NXProject Installer</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Close">Close</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_OpenApp">Open NXProject</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_InstalledOpenWhenReady">✓ NXProject installed. Do Step 3 (AI) if you like, then click "Open NXProject" when ready.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step1Title">Step 1 — .NET 10 Desktop Runtime (approx. 58 MB)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step1Button">Download and install .NET 10</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step1Manual">Download in browser</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step1ManualTip">Opens the .NET 10 installer in your browser to download and install manually.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step2Title">Step 2 — Install NXProject (approx. 2 MB)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step2Status">Downloads the latest version and installs it for your user.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step2Button">Install NXProject</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Retry">Try again</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step3Title">Step 3 (optional): install AI — Windows only</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step3Desc">Windows-ONLY install. If you already use it on WSL, the item shows as installed (WSL) and doesn't need reinstalling.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step3Codex">Codex (OpenAI) — (Recommended Open) (1) — approx. 285 MB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step3Claude">Claude Code (Anthropic) (3) — approx. 309 MB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step3Llama">Local AI (LLaMA — Meta) (2) — approx. 2 GB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step3CodexNote">(1) Has limited free access, with no set deadline at the time of this setup.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step3LlamaNote">(2) Simpler model; runs 100% on your machine (does NOT use the Internet) and needs a more powerful computer. It is downloaded when NXProject opens.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Title">Step 4 (optional): NXProject fields in Azure DevOps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Desc">NXProject stores hours, dates and sync control in Azure DevOps custom fields. Here you detect what already exists and create only what is missing, instead of adding them one by one.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Open">Configure DevOps fields…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Org">Organization</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Server">Server</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ServerTip">Where the NXProject fields will be configured. Only Azure DevOps is implemented today; GitProject (GitHub Projects) is a path under study.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ServerTodoTitle">Not implemented yet</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ServerTodo">Configuring fields on GitProject (GitHub Projects) is not implemented yet — the server goes back to Azure DevOps.&#10;&#10;On GitHub the fields belong to the PROJECT (not to the process) and the EPIC/Feature/Story/Task hierarchy does not exist out of the box: the levels would have to be mapped. The design is in Plano_GitProject_Import_Sync.md, at the repository root.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Project">Project</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Pat">Token (PAT)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PatNote">This token is used ONLY NOW, in this window, to detect and create the fields. The installer does NOT store it, does NOT change the token NXProject uses day to day, and does NOT include it in the exported configuration file — it is gone when you close the window. Creating fields requires process edit permission (Project Collection Administrator).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Loaded">Organization, project, field names and token came from the NXProject already installed on this machine.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4LoadedNoPat">Organization, project and field names came from the installed NXProject. The token was not stored — please enter one.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4CheckingSavedPat">Checking whether the token saved in NXProject can create fields…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4SavedPatOk">Reusing the NXProject token: it can create fields.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4SavedPatNoAccess">The token saved in NXProject CANNOT create fields — enter a PAT with "Work Items — Read, write, &amp; manage" below.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4SavedPatUnknown">Could not check the token saved in NXProject — enter a PAT that can create fields.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PatNoAccess">DevOps refused this token. Creating fields needs a PAT that can administer the process — see below how to generate one.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PatDialogTitle">DevOps refused to create the fields</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PatDialogBody">Creating a field changes the organization PROCESS — the everyday token, which only reads and writes work items, is not enough.&#10;&#10;Both are required:&#10;  • a PAT with the "Work Items — Read, write, &amp; manage" scope (or Full access);&#10;  • your account in the Project Collection Administrators group.&#10;&#10;If the second is missing, no token will do: ask a collection administrator to run this step or to add your account.&#10;&#10;Open your organization's token page now?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PatHelpTitle">How to generate a token that can create fields</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PatHelpSteps">1) In DevOps, top right → User settings → Personal access tokens → New Token.&#10;2) Organization: the same as above. Scope: tick "Work Items — Read, write, &amp; manage" (or use Full access).&#10;3) The account must be a Project Collection Administrator: creating a field changes the process, which is not a regular user permission.&#10;4) Copy the generated token and paste it into the Token (PAT) box above. It is good for this configuration only: it is not stored, it does not replace the NXProject token and it is not shared — feel free to revoke it in DevOps once you are done.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PatHelpLink">Microsoft documentation on Personal Access Tokens</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PrefixHint">The names above are the NXProject defaults and can be changed. Suggestion for a new organization: prefix them with "nx_" (nx_HH_Estimado, nx_Data_Inicio…) so NXProject fields stand out in the field list. If you change them here, use the same names in the NXProject configuration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4UseStdOnTask">on Task use "{0}"</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4UseStdOnType">on {0} use "{1}"</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4SuggestStd">DevOps already has the built-in "{1}" on {0} — tick the option beside it to use that instead of creating a field</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4UseStdOnTaskTip">Tick this if your Task already uses the built-in DevOps date field. NXProject then reads and writes that field ON THE TASK (the Story keeps the custom one), and the installer stops asking to associate the custom field there. The choice is saved to the NXProject configuration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ConfigUpdated">NXProject configuration updated with the Task field choice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ConfigUpdatedNames">NXProject configuration updated: {0} field name(s) and the Task field choice.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Detect">Detect in DevOps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Export">Export .json</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ExportTip">Saves the field names, the Task built-in field choice and which optional features apply to a .json file, to share with your team. The token is NOT exported.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Import">Import .json</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ImportTip">Loads a .json exported by someone else and fills this screen. Organization and project are only filled in if empty here. After importing, run Detect again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Exported">Configuration exported to {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Imported">Configuration imported: {0} field name(s) applied. Run Detect to check against DevOps.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ImportBadFile">This file is not an NXProject field configuration.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Create">Create checked fields</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Detecting">Querying DevOps…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4NeedsConnection">Fill in organization, project and token before detecting.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Ready">already exists, on every work item</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Standard">uses the DevOps built-in field on {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ReadyAlias">already exists in DevOps under the name "{0}"</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ViaAlias">(found as "{0}")</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4NotFound">does not exist — can be created</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4MissingIn">exists, but missing on: {0}</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Conflict">ALREADY EXISTS as {0}, and NXProject needs {1} — pick another name</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4TypeNarrower">exists as {0}; NXProject writes {1} — fractional values (7.5h) will be rounded or refused by DevOps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ConflictCount">{0} name(s) already taken by a field of a different type</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PermOk">permission to create fields: OK</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PermDenied">NO permission to edit the process — creation will fail (Project Collection Administrator required)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PermToken">the token lacks the scope to query permissions — see below how to generate a PAT with access</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4PermUnknown">could not check the permission ({0}) — any error will show when creating</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ProcessInherited">process "{0}" is inherited: it accepts new fields</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ProcessSystem">process "{0}" is a system process and does NOT accept new fields — inherit the process in DevOps first</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4AllOk">every field already exists</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4MissingCount">{0} field(s) to create</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4NothingChecked">No field checked for creation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ConfirmTitle">Create fields in DevOps</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4ConfirmBody">The fields below will be created in process "{0}" and will exist in EVERY project using that process:&#10;&#10;{1}&#10;&#10;No existing field is changed or deleted. Confirm?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Creating">Creating {0}…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4CreateDone">Done: {0} succeeded, {1} with issues — see each field line.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step4Footer">Creation uses the Azure DevOps Process API and only adds fields. Process rules and permissions still apply: if something is refused, the field line shows why.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Setup_Step3ClaudeNote">(3) Claude Code is PAID — requires an Anthropic account/subscription. Robust and widely used tool.</sys:String>
